@@ -3,6 +3,46 @@
 Experimental native-stereo 6DOF OpenVR mod for the 32-bit Steam release of
 Bayonetta (executable timestamp `0x591AD330`).
 
+## Floor and heading calibration (build 20261011.55)
+
+Hold **L3+R3 for one second** on the player-one gamepad, or hold both VR
+thumbstick clicks for one second. F8 performs the same calibration. Keep
+Bayonetta standing on ordinary flat ground and wear the headset at your normal
+playing height. The runtime's configured physical floor must already be correct.
+The shortcut sets eye height from the headset's measured height above that
+floor and levels the game camera. Looking down or tilting your head during
+calibration no longer bakes that tilt into the origin. HUD/movie reanchoring
+remains part of the shortcut.
+
+Both VR processes explicitly request OpenVR standing tracking space, including
+when playing seated. Gamepad calibration also works with `VRControllers=0`;
+that setting controls Touch input emulation. The physical chord is consumed
+while calibration input is active. Holds fire once and reset after focus loss,
+disconnect, or a polling gap. Both eyes use the same calibration and pose.
+
+The game floor reference is the player-one character's feet position
+(Steam pointer VA `05B6075C`, player + `D0`). It is
+not a terrain raycast or verified ground-contact test: do not calibrate during
+a jump. Wall-walking, missing player data, invalid camera matrices or invalid
+head height skip the floor update and log the fallback. Successful calibration
+logs `calibration: floor aligned`. The correction removes current camera
+pitch/roll and applies a height offset; it preserves subsequent game-camera
+movement, so new terrain or changed camera elevation may need recalibration.
+It does not change world scale. `FloorCalibration=0` disables the scene-height
+and leveling correction. The map/movie cinema composition remains intact.
+
+Tests cover 1,575 combinations of camera/head tilt, height and world scale,
+the physical floor plane, stereo/crouch tracking, projection-based camera
+recovery, invalid inputs and controller hold/focus/disconnect behavior.
+Release/Win32, the complete regression suite and companion transport checks
+pass. Both .55 components are installed; the actual game/headset alignment
+still needs user validation. Previous files are saved in
+`.diagnostics/before55-20261011-223031`.
+Installed DLL SHA256:
+`54E9CF238903D0B91F73EBD37F4D5033A886AD0D483BE2A6767F5625E7DE3C77`.
+Installed companion SHA256:
+`D96AC0F59A2456FA1DB4B7BB7E9AD497022D34B386235A0E9DA3246CD67891E7`.
+
